{
  "requirement": "A GitHub Actions CI workflow MUST run, for pull requests and pushes to `main`, these checks: `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace` under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run`, `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`, `mdbook test`, the autofix controller tests with `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`, and, in a separate job, the Symposium session-start hook smoke test `tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`. It also builds the book as documentation under {cite}`requirements.index.render_only`, without requiring collected execution reports for rendering. On a push to `main`, only after every check job passes, it deploys the generated `book/` directory to GitHub Pages. The book MUST set `output.html.site-url` to `/habeas-codicem/` for project-site hosting.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The single marked test, `tests/repository.rs#fn[ci_tests_pull_requests_and_main_then_deploys_the_book_from_main]`, covers each obligation in `requirements.integration.ci`. I read `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `book.toml` only to see what the assertions apply to.\n\n- **Triggers (pull requests and pushes to `main`).** The test asserts the exact `on:` block: `push: branches: [main]` plus `pull_request:`.\n- **Required checks.** It uses `workflow_job` to take the `test-and-build` job. It then asserts that these steps are present and in order:\n  - `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`\n  - `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace`\n  - `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`\n  - `mdbook test`\n- **Coverage gate.** It also asserts the `cargo habeas coverage-check` step. That step has no `if` and no `continue-on-error`, so coverage failures are enforced. The requirement does not state this gate, so it is extra checking.\n- **Symposium smoke test in a separate job.** The test asserts that the `symposium-hook` job runs `python3 tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`. It reads that job separately from `test-and-build`.\n- **Book build.** The test asserts that the `mdbook build` step runs in `test-and-build` and that the pages artifact is uploaded with `path: book`. The `render_only` aspect comes from the `mdbook build` step using the `habeas mdbook` preprocessor and renderer, which `book.toml` configures. The test does not separately assert that rendering needs no execution reports. That is hard to test in a workflow file, and `requirements.index.render_only` has its own tests, so I do not count it as a gap.\n- **Deployment.** The `deploy` job is asserted to have `if: github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'`. It is also asserted to have `needs: [test-and-build, symposium-hook]`, which matches \"only after every check job passes\", and to use `actions/deploy-pages@v4`.\n- **`site-url`.** The test asserts that `book.toml` has `output.habeas.html.site-url` equal to `/habeas-codicem/`. The requirement says `output.html.site-url`. The book's renderer is the custom `habeas` renderer, which wraps the html table, so I read this as the same setting.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating workflow change that these assertions would accept.",
  "references": "a8abf153c89272233a77553f9d744b8b6c5dbba98424eae9956c0f6b77735200",
